---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/shloka-portrait.jpg';
import forest from '../assets/forest.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="About Shloka Iyer, LMFT | South Asian Therapist in San Francisco"
  description="Meet Shloka Iyer, a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist and immigrant based in San Francisco, offering online therapy for adults across California."
  ogType="profile"
>
  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="split__media split__media--portrait arch" data-reveal>
        <Image src={portrait} alt="Shloka Iyer, LMFT" widths={[400, 640, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 22rem, 40vw" loading="eager" quality={75} />
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
        <h1>Understanding ourselves in context.</h1>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p class="lead">I became interested in psychology through close relationships and lived experiences where mental health was present, but not always openly spoken about.</p>
        <p>I also saw how culture shaped the way people understood, expressed, or avoided those experiences, often in ways that weren't immediately visible.</p>
        <p>Those experiences stayed with me. They shaped the way I think about people and the way I practice therapy today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <p>Over time, I came to believe that our struggles rarely exist in isolation. They're influenced by our relationships, the cultures we move through, the expectations we carry, and the environments we adapt to. While these experiences don't define us, they often shape the way we see ourselves and the choices we make.</p>
        <p>My own experience as an immigrant further deepened that perspective. Living between cultures has taught me that identity isn't something we discover once and keep forever. It continues to evolve as our lives, relationships, and environments change. Some questions don't have neat resolutions, but they can become easier to understand and live alongside.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cream section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">My philosophy</p>
        <h2>"What has shaped you?"</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>I don't believe people exist in a vacuum, and I don't think therapy should either.</p>
        <p>It's easy to view emotional difficulties as something that exists solely within the individual. While our internal world matters, so do the contexts we live in: our relationships, culture, communities, work, stage of life, and the responsibilities we carry.</p>
        <p>Rather than asking, "What's wrong with you?", I often find myself asking, "What has shaped you?"</p>
        <p>That question tends to open the door to richer conversations and, more importantly, more compassionate ones.</p>
        <p>For me, therapy isn't about becoming a perfect version of yourself or eliminating every uncomfortable emotion. It's about understanding yourself more honestly, building a greater capacity to navigate life's uncertainties, and making choices that feel aligned with the life you're trying to create.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line" aria-label="How I work">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="features features--three" data-reveal>
        <li class="feature"><Icon name="heart" /><div><h3>Relational &amp; Collaborative</h3><p>We explore together, curiously and at your pace.</p></div></li>
        <li class="feature"><Icon name="chat" /><div><h3>Authentic &amp; Human</h3><p>Real conversations in a space that feels safe and non-judgmental.</p></div></li>
        <li class="feature"><Icon name="context" /><div><h3>Context Matters</h3><p>Your story is shaped by more than just you, and that matters.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">My approach</p>
        <h2>The relationship is part of the work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>One of the most important parts of therapy is the relationship itself.</p>
        <p>Feeling understood doesn't automatically create change, but it often creates the safety to become curious about parts of ourselves that are easier to avoid. That curiosity becomes the starting point for the work we do together.</p>
        <p>My style is conversational, engaged, and, at times, direct. I value authenticity in the therapy room, which means I don't aim to be a blank slate. I bring warmth, curiosity, and humor where it feels appropriate, while maintaining the professional boundaries that allow therapy to remain a meaningful space.</p>
        <p>Above all, I want therapy to feel like a place where you don't have to perform, have all the answers, or arrive with everything figured out. You simply have to be willing to show up.</p>
        <p><a class="arrow-link" href="/approach">More about how I work</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">A little more about me</p>
        <h2>Outside the therapy room</h2>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p>Outside of therapy, you'll usually find me planning my next trip, hiking, or spending time by the ocean, my favorite place to reset. I also have a cat named Oreo, who may occasionally make an appearance during telehealth sessions.</p>
        <p>I enjoy writing about the intersection of identity, culture, relationships, and modern life, and you'll often find those reflections in the <a href="/resources">Resources</a> section of this website.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media arch--soft" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <Image src={forest} alt="" widths={[480, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 40vw" quality={70} style="aspect-ratio:4/5" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Qualifications</p>
        <h2>Training and experience</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I am a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) based in California and provide virtual therapy to adults across the state.</p>
          <p>My clinical work has included community mental health, intensive outpatient and partial hospitalization programs, and private practice. Over the years, I've worked with adults navigating anxiety, depression, life transitions, relationship concerns, identity development, burnout, and cultural adjustment.</p>
          <p>I regularly engage in continuing education and consultation to ensure my work remains thoughtful, current, and responsive to the people I work with.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="rows" style="margin-top:2rem">
          <div><dt>License</dt><dd>Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist, California, LMFT #154641</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Who</dt><dd>Individual therapy for adults (18+)</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Online sessions across California</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Based in San Francisco</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a class="arrow-link" href="/faq#fee">Fees and insurance</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Wondering whether we'd be a good fit?"
    text="I welcome you to schedule a consultation. Finding the right therapeutic relationship is important, and I'm happy to answer any questions you may have before getting started."
  />
</Base>
